02178              *
02179              *THIS FUNCTION PURGES UNWANTED FILES FROM THE DISK, 
02180              *PACKS THE REMAINING FILES, RECLAIMING THE SPACE
02181              *
02182              *PURGE IS DONE IN TWO PASSES
02183              *
02184              *                     PASS 1
02185              *TEST VALIDITY OF INPUT FILE STRING, WRITE DELETED F
02186              *MARKERS IN DIRECTORY FCB OF FILES TO BE PURGED.
02187              *
02188              *                     PASS 2
02189              *SEARCH FOR DELETED FILE MARK (ATTRIBUTE = 80).  ON 
02190              *THE FIRST DELETED FILE MARK, SCAN FORWARD UNTIL A N
02191              *DELETED FILE IS FOUND. THIS FILE IS THEN MOVED INTO
02192              *AREA TO BE PURGED.  THIS PROCESS THEN CONTINUES TO 
02193              *OF THE DIRECTORY. EACH TIME A FILE IS MOVED, THE DI
02194              *IS UPDATED.
02195              *
02196              *                    ERRORS
02197              *SEVERAL ERRORS MAY OCCUR DURING THE PURGE PROCESS, 
02198              *WHICH ARE FATAL TO ALL FILES FOLLOWING THE ERROR.  
02199              *POSSIBLE ERRORS MAY CAUSE DIRECTORY FAULTS.  PURGE 
